From 0bc92253d3fe438e97fb816d192366684a24c224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:45:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] Eden (Doris): bigger stream buffer for uploads;
 pipeline builders on fast cores when shaders are synchronous; shader loop
 limit back to 8192; hitch sampler

- Stream buffer 512 MiB on Android (prefaulted at load), uploads up to half of it go through
  it, and the real GPU progress is read before falling back to (or creating) staging buffers.
  Build 16's longest hitches came with GPU memory jumping 256-576 MiB in 64 MiB blocks and
  falling back within seconds.
- With asynchronous shaders off, pipeline builder threads run at normal priority on the
  performance cores instead of as power-efficient background threads (the Vulkan worker
  waited 55-224 ms per new pipeline).
- Shader loop limit default 8192 (Eden's) instead of PR #4324's 256: the counter is per
  invocation for the whole shader, so nested loops were cut short.
- Async texture removal is also called off when another texture over the same memory is
  created, removed or drawn into meanwhile; pressure threshold 2.45 GiB.
- Report: upload volume, new staging buffers and GPU memory, time getting/freeing GPU memory,
  waiting for the game's commands, game threads' CPU time per hitch; hitch sampler writes
  the GPU thread's stacks during frames over 50 ms to doris_hitches.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
